  "final_message": "Done. The app is implemented and verified:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) \u2014 Flask with SQLite under `./data`:\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 + `token`)\n- `GET /api/me`, `GET /api/me/login-attempts` (20 newest)\n- `GET /api/admin/locks`, `POST /api/admin/locks/{username}/unlock`\n- Lockout: 5 consecutive failures \u2192 429 with `Retry-After` for 15 min; success resets the count.\n- Per-client rate limit: 20 login attempts/minute \u2192 429 with `Retry-After`.\n- Admin account `admin` from `ADMIN_PASSWORD`; sign-in disabled when unset. Tokens via `itsdangerous` with a persistent secret in `data/`.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/src/`) \u2014 React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind (v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`): sign-in/register tabs, signed-in header with sign-out, account page (last login + attempts), and admin locked-users page with Unlock. Lockout/rate-limit failures surface \"try again at \u2026\" messaging.\n\nVerified: full auth/lockout/unlock flow, rate limiting, 401 on missing/invalid tokens, admin-disabled behavior, frontend build (`npm ci && npm run build`), and gunicorn serving both `/api` and `/`. Docker isn't available in the sandbox, so I couldn't run `docker build`, but the Dockerfile already handles the `npm ci`/pip-install/build steps and nothing was changed that would break it.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
